        "## Troubleshooting\n\n"
        "- **Section 1 stops with \"needs a Linux x86_64 runtime\".** The locked environment is built from manylinux "
        "wheels. Use Google Colab, Kaggle or a Linux Jupyter server; Windows and macOS kernels are not supported.\n"
        "- **Section 1 fails while downloading** (`uv` wheel, Python build or packages). The runtime needs PyPI and the "
        "python-build-standalone download; run the cell again once the network is back. A \"size/SHA-256\" or \"does not "
        "match its digest\" error means a file was altered: do not edit the cell, regenerate the notebook from the "
        "repository.\n"
        "- **A restart prompt.** This notebook never needs a runtime restart: nothing is installed into the kernel. If the "
        "runtime restarted anyway (you chose it, or it was reset), choose **Run all** again from the top; files already "
        "downloaded and verified are reused while they are still there.\n"
        "- **\"The isolated environment's Python process exited\".** Usually the runtime ran out of memory. Restart the "
        "session and choose **Run all**; on CPU, close other notebooks first.\n"
        "- **Section 3 or 4 stops on a download** (the Hub snapshot or the tarball). The Hub was unreachable or the transfer "
        "was cut; run the cell again later. Files already verified are kept under `weights/` and are not fetched twice.\n"
        "- **A digest or size mismatch in Section 3 or 4.** A download was incomplete or altered; the notebook refuses it "
        "rather than continuing. Run the cell again; never edit the manifest or the pinned digests.\n"
        "- **Out of disk.** The tarball needs about 4 GB of free disk, the locked install a few GB more. Start a fresh "
        "runtime, or delete `dimer_isolated_env/` and `weights/levir-cd/` from an earlier attempt.\n"
        "- **BYOD is refused in Section 4.** The message names what to fix: fewer than 7 distinct pairs, a zip with more "
        "than 6,001 files or more than 512 MB uncompressed, a missing `pairs.csv` or column, a file named in `pairs.csv` "
        "that is not in the zip (or matches several files), dates of different sizes, a side outside 64..2,048 or not a "
        "multiple of 32, or a label value other than 0 / 255. Fix the set and run Section 4 with **Run after** again. An "
        "empty or cancelled upload asks you to choose one file or set `BYOD_PATH`.\n"
        "- **Section 7 or 8 stops with a message about the kept epoch or reload parity.** The model in memory is not the "
        "one the history or the artifact describes — usually a cell was re-run out of order. Run Section 6 with **Run after** "
        "(it starts from the pretrained model), or restart the session and choose **Run all**.\n"
        "- **Numbers differ slightly from the recorded runs.** GPU float16 arithmetic is not bit-for-bit the CPU's: a "
        "difference of 0.0001 in a precision or a validation loss between a T4 and a CPU run is expected, and on a GPU a "
        "trained epoch whose validation loss is within that difference of epoch 0 can be kept instead. Larger differences on "
        "the default settings mean a form field was changed.\n\n"
        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **Bi-temporal pair:** two images of the same place taken at two dates, `before` and `after`.\n"
        "- **Co-registered:** aligned so the same pixel shows the same ground position in both images.\n"
        "- **Change map:** the network's `tanh` output in (−1, 1) per pixel; not a calibrated probability.\n"
        "- **Binary mask / threshold:** changed where the change map exceeds 0.5 (the upstream rule).\n"
        "- **Ignore class:** label value −1, pixels excluded from every metric.\n"
        "- **All-unchanged baseline:** predicting \"unchanged\" everywhere; its accuracy is the unchanged fraction and its F1 "
        "and IoU are 0.\n"
        "- **F1 / IoU / precision / recall:** changed-class scores over the pooled labelled pixels; F1 is the harmonic mean "
        "of precision and recall, IoU the overlap of predicted and labelled change divided by their union.\n"
        "- **Content decoder / focuser / change decoder:** the per-date decoders that keep scene content, the module that "
        "turns their disagreement into change weights, and the decoder that outputs the change map (the only part trained by "
        "default).\n"
        "- **Content-consistency terms:** the part of the upstream loss that compares cosine similarities of randomly drawn "
        "pixel pairs within each date; the source of the draw noise.\n"
        "- **Epoch / epoch 0:** one pass over the training pairs; epoch 0 is the frozen checkpoint, scored before any "
        "training so it can win.\n"
        "- **Validation loss / draw seed:** the selection criterion, computed on the validation pairs with the content-term "
        "pixel pairs drawn from a fixed seed so every epoch is scored on the same draw.\n"
        "- **Training / validation / test split:** pairs used to train, to choose the epoch, and to report the final result "
        "once; here the dataset's own splits.\n"
        "- **Adapter / reload parity:** the saved tensors of the kept epoch, and the check that a pipeline rebuilt from them "
        "gives the same change maps and metrics.\n\n"
